1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
When it came time to cross the ocean,

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:04,160
why was the strongest Hanuman silent?

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,103
The same Hanuman,

4
00:00:07,103 --> 00:00:09,582
who had flown to the sun in his childhood.

5
00:00:09,582 --> 00:00:12,710
And a similar question was asked by Shri Ram himself.

6
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:16,368
[Ram] When Bali took everything from Sugriva,

7
00:00:16,368 --> 00:00:18,010
why didn't Hanuman stop Bali?

8
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,140
Maharishi Agastya said...

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,777
[Agastya] Ram,

10
00:00:21,777 --> 00:00:23,330
there was a curse behind it.

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,184
Fearless from boons,

12
00:00:25,184 --> 00:00:28,380
that child began to cause havoc in the sages' ashrams.

13
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,010
He would scatter sacrificial vessels and overturn piles of bark clothes.

14
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:35,140
The sages endured. Then one day...

15
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,670
[Rishi] The strength you rely on to torment us,

16
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:39,790
you will not remember it for a long time.

17
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,026
[Rishi] When you remember it,

18
00:00:43,026 --> 00:00:44,500
only then will it be of use.

19
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,174
And from that day,

20
00:00:46,174 --> 00:00:47,740
that child became quiet.

21
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,384
Years later, in search of Sita,

22
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:52,390
the Vanaras reached the seashore.

23
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,601
Before them lay an ocean of a hundred yojanas,

24
00:00:55,601 --> 00:00:57,410
about twelve hundred kilometers.

25
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,261
Some said ten yojanas, some fifty.

26
00:01:01,261 --> 00:01:03,156
Angad said, I can go across,

27
00:01:03,156 --> 00:01:05,390
but I'm not sure about returning.

28
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,370
And Hanuman sat there silently.

29
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,596
The one who had to cross this ocean,

30
00:01:10,596 --> 00:01:12,400
he himself did not remember it.

31
00:01:13,270 --> 00:01:15,170
[Jambavan] Hanuman, why are you silent?

32
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,956
[Jambavan] You are the son of the wind,

33
00:01:18,956 --> 00:01:20,719
like Garuda in speed. Arise,

34
00:01:20,719 --> 00:01:21,790
cross this ocean.

35
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:25,018
And as soon as he was reminded of his power,

36
00:01:25,018 --> 00:01:26,220
the curse was broken.

37
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,774
Hanuman's body began to grow,

38
00:01:28,774 --> 00:01:31,220
and Mount Mahendra trembled at his roar.

39
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,470
He did not lack strength; he only lacked someone to remind him.

40
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,360
But in the middle of the ocean,

41
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,280
who was there to block his path?

42
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,360
In the next story.

